ENGLISH:
🚩 ASSIGNMENT: MULTI-BRANCH ORGANIZATION MANAGEMENT SYSTEM (GRADEUP CORE)
1. Required Entities

You are required to design database tables to manage the following:

Organizations:
Each client is treated as a separate tenant (organization) in a multi-tenant system.
Departments:
One organization can have multiple departments (1–N relationship).
Employees:
Each department can have multiple employees (1–N relationship).
Each employee has a detailed profile (1–1 relationship).
Projects:
Projects that are executed within an organization.
Skills:
A catalog of skills (e.g., React, SQL, AI, Running, etc.).
Assignments (ProjectAssignments):
Represents the participation of employees in projects.
An employee can join multiple projects, and a project can have multiple employees (N–N relationship).
EmployeeSkills:
Represents the skills of employees.
One employee can have multiple skills, and one skill can belong to multiple employees (N–N relationship).
2. Required Relationships

Your design must clearly represent the following relationships:

🔹 One-to-One (1–1)
Employees ↔ EmployeeProfiles
Split into separate tables to improve performance and scalability.
🔹 One-to-Many (1–N)
Organizations → Departments → Employees
One organization has many departments.
One department has many employees.
🔹 Many-to-Many (N–N)**
Employees ↔ Projects
Implemented via a junction table: ProjectAssignments
Employees ↔ Skills
Implemented via a junction table: EmployeeSkills
🔹 Self-Referencing Relationship
Employees (Manager_ID)
Each employee may have a manager.
Manager_ID references another record in the Employees table.
Used to model hierarchical structures (manager–subordinate relationships).
🎯 Goal

Design a scalable and normalized relational database that:

Supports multi-tenant architecture
Ensures data integrity and consistency
Handles complex relationships efficiently
Is ready for real-world systems such as HRM, ERP, or enterprise platforms


TIẾNG VIỆT
🚩 ĐỀ BÀI: HỆ THỐNG QUẢN TRỊ TỔ CHỨC ĐA CHI NHÁNH (GRADEUP CORE)
1. Yêu cầu các thực thể (Entities)
Bạn cần thiết kế các bảng để quản lý:

Organizations (Tổ chức): Mỗi khách hàng là một Tenant (Tổ chức) riêng biệt.

Departments (Phòng ban): Một tổ chức có nhiều phòng ban (1-n).

Employees (Nhân sự): Một phòng ban có nhiều nhân viên (1-n). Mỗi nhân viên có một hồ sơ chi tiết (1-1).

Projects (Dự án): Các dự án chạy trong tổ chức.

Skills (Kỹ năng): Danh mục kỹ năng (React, SQL, AI, Running...).

Assignments (Phân công): Nhân viên tham gia vào nhiều dự án, một dự án có nhiều nhân viên (n-n).

Employee_Skills: Một nhân viên có nhiều kỹ năng, một kỹ năng có thể thuộc về nhiều nhân viên (n-n).

2. Các mối quan hệ bắt buộc phải thể hiện
1 - 1: Employees ↔ EmployeeProfiles (Chia bảng để tối ưu hóa hiệu năng).

1 - n: Organizations → Departments → Employees.

n - n (Quan hệ nhiều - nhiều):

Employees ↔ Projects (Thông qua bảng trung gian ProjectAssignments).

Employees ↔ Skills (Thông qua bảng trung gian EmployeeSkills).

Self-referencing (Quan hệ tự thân): Employees (Manager_Id) trỏ về chính bảng Employees để quản lý cấp trên - cấp dưới.